{"title":"Division Algorithm","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>For any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, there exist unique integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93cec0fdda353f0eaec7d2d9d38af18ac5cfdb5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = qb + r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223028f3e44fb9851d57fcf0bd00b009c5bd6903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq r &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Division_Algorithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Existence: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba08047d1e4568402a35807e9c6058657484f7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\{a-nb\\mid n\\in \\mathbb{Z}\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" /> The intersection of the sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is non-empty and has a positive element (take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/505050b3a2b9ed3f539020ad25f3c4941862ee2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=-|a|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />). By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Well_Ordering_Principle\" title=\"Well Ordering Principle\">Well Ordering Principle</a> , it contains a least element. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> equal the value of the least element and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> equal the respective value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14ee5a3e0380c1549433aefee25dd4bf9043f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=a-qb\\Rightarrow a=qb+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"190\" height=\"16\" />. Now we prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42ae5282c8fd37b86e47b2df3959cf8a6b00917d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq r&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> by contradiction. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a18f7fd295a03f9e5a767c79eca4a54178d518b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\geq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff0bb6ce631b0221f0a6df50967f134550963bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=a-qb\\Rightarrow r-b=a-(q+1)b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />. However, this leads to a contradiction (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is supposed to be the smallest positive value that can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/babbc96018c45a0ff8aeda0bcf7fc77dc26a7f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-nb$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cb56cc54d20251e4e097ee2aab2b243941981f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is smaller, positive, and can also be expressed in this manner). Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42ae5282c8fd37b86e47b2df3959cf8a6b00917d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq r&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Uniqueness: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bde3af514487161175e805e5a2d5bd3dd57e25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=qb+r=q&#39;b+r&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"19\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d43e1dc576039dff819ff0e888834b062b3c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$qb+r=q&#39;b+r&#39;\\Rightarrow (r-r&#39;)=b(q&#39;-q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"304\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e334099a70e22d1a228793f5fb26d0acb64990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|r-r&#39;|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. However, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42ae5282c8fd37b86e47b2df3959cf8a6b00917d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq r&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42ae5282c8fd37b86e47b2df3959cf8a6b00917d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq r&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/27036a977b514a47f91146fe83ddd820ca68053d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq |r-r&#39;|&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. The only multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e334099a70e22d1a228793f5fb26d0acb64990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|r-r&#39;|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> can equal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797445485a9120525569647d7ac673a2de426500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|r-r&#39;|=0\\Rightarrow r=r&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342a657d3aa43e75b3194b015fcbf5ad3ca5bf3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\not= 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb88641cdc9533e6198f6b3f5a59c84ef26de277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|q&#39;-q|=0\\Rightarrow q=q&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Divisibility\">Divisibility</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Division_Algorithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Divisibility\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f80eefb2e2c9d1a6762a1a60c136a18e752631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=qb+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400365c088499af977542271fc6363b086a63499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=0$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then we say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/2778132ab31aa1deb3bd4268f7322656fd3b4b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\mid a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> or \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />\". Note that every integer divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Division_Algorithm&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018083032\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 201/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 